 margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; line-height: 28.8px; overflow-wrap: break-word; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font dir=\"auto\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; vertical-align: inherit;\">Does it seem too dry? Maybe, but this way you have a framework to follow and the anxiety will go away as you write. 😉</font></p><p class=\"\" style=\"margin-top: 1rem; margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; line-height: 28.8px; overflow-wrap: break-word; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font dir=\"auto\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; vertical-align: inherit;\">If you want, you can help yourself by inserting the corresponding heading tags (h2, h3) before each paragraph, which will be invaluable when you fix the formatting.</font></p><h1 style=\"font-size: 57.6px; margin: 2rem 0px; font-family: Poppins; line-height: 72.2534px; letter-spacing: -4.032px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font dir=\"auto\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; vertical-align: inherit;\">Write down the details</font></h1><p class=\"\" style=\"margin-top: 1rem; margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; line-height: 28.8px; overflow-wrap: break-word; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font dir=\"auto\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; vertical-align: inherit;\">Breaking your content down into steps is already very useful; you know which direction to take without forgetting anything. Why don\'t you do better?</font></p><p class=\"\" style=\"margin-top: 1rem; margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; line-height: 28.8px; overflow-wrap: break-word; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font dir=\"auto\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; vertical-align: inherit;\">For example, by further breaking down each paragraph and inserting a taste of what you intend to say.</font></p><p class=\"\" style=\"margin-top: 1rem; margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; line-height: 28.8px; overflow-wrap: break-word; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><strong style=\"font-weight: bold; overflow-wrap: brea